    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0328" n="212" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg212"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.569/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tobin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-11-23T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 23,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>58. Your no. 64, November 22, 6 p.m. The Department is gratified to learn that
                    the Cabinet has decided unanimously to recommend the acceptance of the proposed
                    convention. You are informed confidentially that our negotiations with Great
                    Britain are believed to be proceeding favorably; the Department will advise you
                    promptly regarding the progress of those negotiations.</p>
                <p>In your own negotiations with the Government of the Netherlands you will be sure
                    that the change amending the text contained in the <pb facs="0329" n="213"
                        xml:id="pg213"/> Department’s no. 52, October 22, (see Department’s no. 34
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">54</hi>], November 7, repeated to you from
                        London<anchor n="64" xml:id="d128-f1"/>) is incorporated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
